{
  "_meta": {
    "table": "infant_additives",
    "version": "0.1",
    "purpose": "D-140 phase 3: 5(2) of the FSS (Foods for Infant Nutrition) Regulations 2020, \"Only the food additives listed under these regulations shall be used\", one list per product type, plus Schedule I(d)'s nutrient carriers, which each type's (b) allows. Used by lenses/infant.py, in shadow: an INS number on a pack's list that isn't in its type's list is said as \"not found in the list\", never \"not permitted\" (carry-over additives are allowed by 5(2), and the type may be misread; a reviewer confirms).",
    "source": {
      "title": "FSS (Foods for Infant Nutrition) Regulations, 2020, compendium Version II (04.01.2024)",
      "url": "https://fssai.gov.in/docs/food-law/regulations/Comp_IFR_VERSION-II_04_01_2024.pdf",
      "read_on": "2026-09-30",
      "how": "Every row copied by hand from the page images (the text layer merges table cells), PDF page numbers."
    },
    "rules": [
      "`ins` is as printed; lenses/infant.py reads it with core/tokenize.ins_numbers (the one INS parser) and compares on the number and any letter suffix, not roman sub-numbers (the parser keeps a lone 'i' but drops 'ii').",
      "`max` is the regulation's words; a shared cell is repeated on each row it covers. Not compared with anything: labels don't print additive amounts.",
      "Traditional foods (11(2), PDF p. 29): \"If required, the food additives specified for milk cereal based complementary food under these regulations may be used.\""
    ]
  },
